<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<alert xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:emergency:cap:1.2">
    <identifier>urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0c2394f8a094c2254e198dfb98cbdff3c377edb5.001.1</identifier>
    <sender>w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov</sender>
    <sent>2025-07-30T18:57:00-05:00</sent>
    <status>Actual</status>
    <msgType>Alert</msgType>
    <scope>Public</scope>
    <code>IPAWSv1.0</code>
    <info>
        <language>en-US</language>
        <category>Met</category>
        <event>Special Weather Statement</event>
        <responseType>Execute</responseType>
        <urgency>Expected</urgency>
        <severity>Moderate</severity>
        <certainty>Observed</certainty>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>SAME</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <eventCode>
            <valueName>NationalWeatherService</valueName>
            <value>SPS</value>
        </eventCode>
        <effective>2025-07-30T18:57:00-05:00</effective>
        <onset>2025-07-30T18:57:00-05:00</onset>
        <expires>2025-07-30T19:45:00-05:00</expires>
        <senderName>NWS Huntsville AL</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued July 30 at 6:57PM CDT by NWS Huntsville AL</headline>
        <description>At 656 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Loretto, or 15 miles northeast of Florence, moving southwest at 5
mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Florence, Killen, Lexington, St. Florian, Underwood-Petersville,
Green Hill, Center Star, Zip City, Kingtown, and Ford City.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.

Frequent cloud to ground lightning is occurring with this storm.
Lightning can strike 10 miles away from a thunderstorm. Seek a safe
shelter inside a building or vehicle.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SPSHUN</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>WMOidentifier</valueName>
            <value>WWUS84 KHUN 302357</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>NWSheadline</valueName>
            <value>A STRONG THUNDERSTORM WILL IMPACT NORTHEASTERN LAUDERDALE AND EAST CENTRAL COLBERT COUNTIES THROUGH 745 PM CDT</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>eventMotionDescription</valueName>
            <value>2025-07-30T23:56:00-00:00...storm...038DEG...6KT...35.0,-87.49</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>maxWindGust</valueName>
            <value>40 MPH</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>maxHailSize</valueName>
            <value>0.00</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
