        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued July 30 at 7:24PM CDT by NWS Topeka KS</headline>
        <description>At 723 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Burdick, moving north at 25 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down small tree limbs and blow
around unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Herington, Wilsey, and Burdick.
</description>
