        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued July 30 at 6:33PM MDT by NWS Cheyenne WY</headline>
        <description>At 632 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 9
miles east of Evansville, or 13 miles east of Casper, moving
northeast at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and nickel size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Glenrock.

This includes Interstate 25 in Wyoming between mile markers 163 and
175.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Heavy rain is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
