        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued July 30 at 5:57PM PDT by NWS Boise ID</headline>
        <description>At 557 PM PDT, Doppler radar was tracking a cluster of strong
thunderstorms near Mustang Butte, or 14 miles southeast of Rome,
moving northwest at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Areas of blowing dust reducing
visibilities. Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible.

This strong thunderstorm will be near...
Scott Reservoir around 710 PM MDT.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.

Torrential rainfall is also occurring with this storm and may lead to
localized flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded
roadways.</instruction>
